420,/Azande_Baxter_1953_17_KS,CentralAfrica,Azande,blood-brothers,kin_role,blood-brothers,kin_role,kinship,"Text states blood-brothers have licensed chaffing; a recurrent, institutionalized teasing tied to kin role.","Evans-Pritchard, 16, 1933; blood-brothers have licence, which is not permitted to others, to chaff each other freely in this way.",licence to chaff,,symmetric,insulting_license,0.85,,2026-07-06T08:56:40.407242+00:00
421,/Azande_Baxter_1953_76_KS,CentralAfrica,Azande,blood-brothers,kin_role,blood-brothers,kin_role,kinship,Text states blood-brothers stand to each other in a joking relationship; kin-role based licensed abuse.,"The behaviour which blood-brothers are expected to assume towards each other is the opposite of that required towards kin and in-laws, and they stand to each other in a sort of joking relationship. They abuse each other with impunity, saying things that would normally be considered causes of deep quarrels.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T08:57:06.488410+00:00
422,/Azande_Baxter_1953_76_KS,CentralAfrica,Azande,bakulemi,clan,bakulemi,clan,within_group,Joking relationship extended in modified form to clansmen (bakulemi) — intra-societal clan-patterned teasing.,"In a modified form this joking relationship is extended to clansmen, known as bakulemi; and between certain clans, such as the Abanvra, Abangombi, Akalinga, and Agiti, a permanent joking relationship has grown up.",,bakulemi,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.85,,2026-07-06T08:57:06.488410+00:00
