978,/Somali_Helander_1988_160_KS,EasternAfrica,Somali,nobles,group,commoners,group,within_group,"Text describes recurrent, culturally patterned pejorative joking by nobles toward commoners within the society.","The commoners are often talked about in contemptuous ways. Nearly all of the terms used for them are also pejoratives. ... Still, many of these terms, as well as their exegesis, are considered highly amusing by the nobles.",pejorative joking / degradation,"jareer, timo adag",non_symmetric,insulting_license,0.9,"Gesture (twisting hair) and specific terms indicate culturally recognized, recurrent teasing by nobles toward commoners.",2026-07-06T09:56:47.626260+00:00
493,/BerbersofMorocco_Coon_1931_116_KS,NorthernAfrica,BerbersofMorocco,Gzennaya,regional group,students from the Jebala,regional group,cross_group,"Recurrent, culturally patterned teasing by Gzennaya/Riffians directed at Jebala students, causing their exclusion.","Before European occupation, these western students did not meet with a warm reception in the Rif. They were frequently refused entrance to some districts. In others, so many jokes were played upon them that they left hurriedly and never returned.
On one occasion, Jebalan students entered the mosque in a canton of the Gzennaya, leaving outside a mule which they had brought with them.",practical joking/exclusion,,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.8,Text reports generalized pattern of jokes played on Jebala students by Riffian districts including Gzennaya; extracted canton name as actor.,2026-07-06T09:04:50.763453+00:00
494,/BerbersofMorocco_Coon_1931_134_KS,NorthernAfrica,BerbersofMorocco,men,group,women,group,within_group,Festival grape‑picking features recurrent licensed joking/play between men and women during weddings.,"Grape picking is a season of carnival; the people sleep in the vineyards, and after and between intervals in weddings the men and women go up to the vineyards, where they joke, shout and shoot off guns, and play games; the men wrestle together, and the women and men form sides and throw stones at each other.",seasonal/carnival licensed joking,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.7,,2026-07-06T09:04:59.734166+00:00
495,/BerbersofMorocco_Coon_1931_141_KS,NorthernAfrica,BerbersofMorocco,The Riffians,ethnic group,the Senhajans,ethnic group,cross_group,Ethnographer reports Riffians telling a recurrent joke about Senhajans—cross-ethnic teasing.,"The Riffians tell the story as a joke on the Senhajans, and although this circumstance does not necessarily render the tale false it does not increase its chances of being true.",a joke on,,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.8,Text frames this as Riffians' joking about Senhajans; directionality implied.,2026-07-06T09:05:06.894393+00:00
