1200,/san_marshall_20_1957_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,Ego,kin_role,sibling of same sex,kin_role,kinship,"Text states same-sex siblings are permitted joking, a patterned kin-role rule.",The sibling category is divided on the basis of sex. Ego jokes with a sibling of the same sex as his own and is prohibited from joking with a sibling of opposite sex.,,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.95,,2026-07-06T10:16:08.526575+00:00
1201,/san_marshall_20_1957_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,Ego,kin_role,cousins (consanguineous kin classified by generation),kin_role,kinship,Consanguineous kin may be classified by generation and included in jokings (cousins explicitly cited).,"Consanguineous kin may be so classified by generation (i.e. cousins) as shown in Diagram 1, or by the factor of the name, i.e. the person for whom ego is named or persons named for ego.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:16:08.526575+00:00
1202,/san_marshall_20_1957_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,Ego,kin_role,name-relatives (persons named for ego or for whom ego is named),kin_role,kinship,Text describes joking with persons placed in same category by name (homonymous classification).,"Ego has the joking relationship with anyone of either sex who is classified with himself or herself, to whom ego applies the term !gu!na (or tun!ga w.s.) or tũn. ... or by the factor of the name, i.e. the person for whom ego is named or persons named for ego.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:16:08.526575+00:00
1203,/san_marshall_20_1957_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,Ego,kin_role,grandparents,kin_role,kinship,Grandparents are explicitly listed as persons with whom ego may joke unless naming places them otherwise.,"Ego has the joking relationship with grandparents and grandchildren unless the factor of the name places ego terminologically in the other, non-joking, division.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:16:08.526575+00:00
1204,/san_marshall_20_1957_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,Ego,kin_role,grandchildren,kin_role,kinship,Grandchildren included in joking set unless naming places them in non-joking division.,"Ego has the joking relationship with grandparents and grandchildren unless the factor of the name places ego terminologically in the other, non-joking, division.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:16:08.526575+00:00
