1212,/san_marshall_20_1957_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,Ego,kin_role,persons termed !gu!na or tun!ga w.s. or tũn,kin_role,kinship,The text defines these terms as the classificatory labels whose bearers have joking relations with ego.,"Ego has the joking relationship with anyone of either sex who is classified with himself or herself, to whom ego applies the term !gu!na (or tun!ga w.s.) or tũn.",,!gu!na; tun!ga w.s.; tũn,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.95,,2026-07-06T10:16:08.526575+00:00
1213,/san_marshall_213_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,kin_role,!gun!a (or tũn!ga w.s.) and tũn,kin_role,kinship,Text states ego has a joking relationship with anyone he terms !gun!a/tũn (kin-role based).,Ego applies the terms !gun!a (or tũn!ga w.s.) and tũn to persons in his own generation and in generations alternate to his own; he has the joking relationship with anyone to whom he applies these terms.,,"!gun!a, tũn, tũn!ga",symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:16:14.682544+00:00
1214,/san_marshall_214_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,kin_role,affines,kin_role,kinship,Text states affinal relationships include a continuing 'joking status' with ego; institutionalized kin joking.,"A !Kung calls his affines mi twisi.

Once established, an affinal relationship is considered to be indissoluble even though the person through whom the relationship with ego was brought about be dead or divorced. For example, should ego's brother die, his brother's wife remains in affinal relationship with ego, and the application of a kin term and the joking status with her continue to be the same as if ego's brother were alive.",joking status with affines,mi twisi,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:16:22.139346+00:00
1215,/san_marshall_214_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,kin_role,brother's wife,kin_role,kinship,Example explicitly says ego retains 'joking status' with his brother's wife even after brother's death.,"For example, should ego's brother die, his brother's wife remains in affinal relationship with ego, and the application of a kin term and the joking status with her continue to be the same as if ego's brother were alive.",joking status with brother's wife,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.95,,2026-07-06T10:16:22.139346+00:00
1216,/san_marshall_216_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,SiHu,kin_role,ego,kin_role,kinship,Affinal reciprocal terms with maintained joking consistency between ego and SiHu (affinal pair).,"For example, a man terms his SiHu tũn!ga; to that man ego is WiBr, who is also termed tũn!ga.",reciprocal affinal terms / joking consistency,tũn!ga,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:16:33.824752+00:00
