1219,/san_marshall_216_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,WiFa,kin_role,DaHu,kin_role,kinship,"Man terms his WiFa ≠tum and is himself DaHu to that man, both termed ≠tum; indicates reciprocal joking/term pair.","A man terms his WiFa ≠tum; he is DaHu to that man, also termed ≠tum.",,≠tum,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:16:33.824752+00:00
1220,/san_marshall_216_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,HuFa,kin_role,SoWi,kin_role,kinship,"A woman HuFa is ≠tum while she is SoWi to him, who terms her /utsu — reciprocal affinal joking terms indicated.","A woman HuFa is ≠tum; she is SoWi to him, termed /utsu.",,≠tum; /utsu,mixed,joking_relationship,0.85,Different term used by each side (/utsu vs ≠tum) but relationship described as reciprocal in terms and joking.,2026-07-06T10:16:33.824752+00:00
1221,/san_marshall_217_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,!hoa,kin_role,tsau,kin_role,kinship,Text states these affinal terms (husband/wife) allow joking between them.,"!Hoa and tsau are the two affinal terms (mentioned earlier) which, along with !gun!a (“big [old] name”) and !guma (“small [young] name”), are the only !Kung Kinship Terminology terms that are words rather than terms specific to kinship. !Hoa is the !Kung word for “man,” and tsau the !Kung word for “woman.” As kin terms they are used only between husband and wife.",allows joking,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:16:59.159897+00:00
