1293,/san_marshall_263_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,co-wives,kin_role,co-wives,kin_role,kinship,Text states co-wives have a recurring joking relationship and use special kin terms for each other.,"Marriage to the same man gives co-wives the joking relationship, and they do not observe the sitting or the name avoidance, though they may have observed those avoidances and may have avoided joking before marriage. Co-wives apply the kin terms !kwi or tsĩ (sister) to each other, or, if they have the same name, they apply the terms !gun!a and !guma.",joking relationship,!kwi; tsĩ; !gun!a; !guma; !gwa di,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:21:12.637687+00:00
1294,/san_marshall_265_1965_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,old men,kin_role,the girl,kin_role,kinship,Text explicitly names a culturally recognized joking relationship between old men and the girl during menstruation rites.,"The two old men should be free from even the most attenuated, symbolic extension of the incest taboo with respect to the girl, and it follows that they should have what is called the joking relationship with her.",joking relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.95,,2026-07-06T10:21:16.803215+00:00
1295,/san_marshall_275_1965_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,wife's brother's wife,kin_role,husband's sister's husband,kin_role,kinship,Text links marriage prohibition to a recurring 'joking relationship' between these affinal kin roles.,Marriage with the wife's brother's wife or the husband's sister's husband is also forbidden; the reason for this lies in a complexity of the joking relationship.,,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.6,Document names the joking relationship as the reason for prohibition but does not specify directional or symmetric privileges.,2026-07-06T10:21:24.447831+00:00
1296,/san_marshall_278_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,kinswoman,kin_role,bride,kin_role,kinship,Text names a culturally recognized 'joking relationship' held by kinswomen toward the bride in wedding rules.,"Any kinswoman (preferably a young one) who is tall enough and strong enough, whether she herself is married or not, and whether or not she has the joking relationship with the bride, may carry the bride and any may attend her.",joking relationship,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.8,,2026-07-06T10:21:34.519749+00:00
1297,/san_marshall_278_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,guest of mature years,group,bride,kin_role,kinship,Guests' permissive seating depends on having a recurrent 'joking relationship' with the bride (institutionalized teasing/licensed familiarity).,Guests of mature years might go and sit by the wedding fire only if they have the joking relationship with both the bride and the groom.,joking relationship,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.8,,2026-07-06T10:21:34.519749+00:00
