1313,/san_marshall_342_1959_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,person,WiBrWi,kin_role,kinship,Text states ego is constrained from joking with WiBrWi and thus avoidance is an institutional rule linked to marriage prohibitions.,"In the sibling category among affines ego is prohibited from marrying only WiBrWi or HuSiHu. ... As we list ego's siblings and affines in Fig. 4 we see that WiBrWi and HuSiHu are the only ones whose sex is opposite to ego's, making marriage possible, but with whom ego is constrained from joking because he does not joke with his WiBr or HuSi, according the same joking status to both members of a married couple.",avoidance / constrained from joking,,symmetric,avoidance,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:22:49.161060+00:00
1314,/san_marshall_342_1959_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,person,HuSiHu,kin_role,kinship,HuSiHu is explicitly identified as a kin-role with which ego is constrained from joking (institutionalized avoidance tied to incest rules).,"In the sibling category among affines ego is prohibited from marrying only WiBrWi or HuSiHu. ... As we list ego's siblings and affines in Fig. 4 we see that WiBrWi and HuSiHu are the only ones whose sex is opposite to ego's, making marriage possible, but with whom ego is constrained from joking because he does not joke with his WiBr or HuSi, according the same joking status to both members of a married couple.",avoidance / constrained from joking,,symmetric,avoidance,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:22:49.161060+00:00
1315,/san_marshall_343_1959_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,ego,kin_role,name relatives classified as grandparents,kin_role,kinship,"Text states ego may joke with name-relatives classified as grandparents; this is recurrent, culturally patterned.","They may joke with name relatives whose names classify them with grandparents, a sibling of the same sex, or the spouse.",may joke,name relationship,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:22:59.281517+00:00
