1327,/san_shostak_269_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,the men of the village,group,girls approaching puberty,age_set,within_group,"Recurring, culturally patterned teasing by village men toward adolescent girls during maturation rituals.","As a girl begins to mature, the men of the village offer running commentaries on the changes in her body—obvious in a culture where the breasts are not covered—and joke about wanting to marry her or to run away with her.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.7,"Pattern described as recurrent and culturally normative; females respond with laughter, indicating licensed teasing.",2026-07-06T10:23:54.393805+00:00
1328,/san_shostak_306_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,a young woman,age_set,an older woman,age_set,within_group,"Text describes recurrent, culturally recognized teasing between younger and older women as a joking relationship.","Between two people who have a joking relationship, the following scene might transpire. A young woman walks into the village with a bright strand of beads around her neck. An older woman sees them and jokes, “Oh, those beads are already mine! Your past stinginess is going to be turned around today!”",joking relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.7,,2026-07-06T10:24:05.302934+00:00
1329,/san_shostak_306_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,in-laws,kin_role,respect relationship (older woman and her target),kin_role,kinship,Describes patterned teasing/laments between in-laws (a kin-based 'respect relationship') leading to reciprocal gift exchanges.,"If the two women are in-laws and have a respect relationship, the situation will be somewhat different. The older woman might sit in her hut and talk loudly to herself: “Does youth need anything to make it beautiful? How is it no one helps this old woman's heart feel young again?”",respect relationship,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.8,Text frames this as a culturally patterned interaction between affinal kin rather than casual individual joking.,2026-07-06T10:24:05.302934+00:00
