1332,/san_silberbauer_143_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,same-sex siblings,kin_role,each other (sibling dyad),kin_role,kinship,"Author states all kin are joking except parents and opposite-sex siblings, implying same-sex siblings occupy joking relations.","In general, all kin are in a joking relationship except one's parents and opposite-sex siblings and their classificatory and fictional equivalents, who are in the avoidance/respect category.",joking relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.85,Entity_b uses phrasing 'each other' to indicate dyadic reciprocal relation among same-sex siblings.,2026-07-06T10:24:27.419146+00:00
