1347,/san_silberbauer_149_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,n//odima,kin_role,n//odisa,kin_role,kinship,Text identifies the n//odima–n//odisa (cross-cousin) pair as a culturally recognized joking relationship.,"What did emerge was that all first marriages (as distinct from subsequent marriages of widowed or divorced persons) had been between boys and girls in a n//odima-n//odisa relationship, which is the terminological equivalent of cross-cousinship and, hence, placed the two in a joking relationship.",joking relationship,n//odima-n//odisa,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:25:19.449969+00:00
1348,/san_silberbauer_151_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,a boy,kin_role,"babama (MB, FZH)",kin_role,kinship,Text states boy and babama are 'joking kin' prior to becoming avoidance affines.,"According to my informants, a boy would treat his babama (MB, FZH) and his ma:sa (fz, mbw) as avoidance kin as soon as he began to court their daughter, anticipating their conversion from joking kin to avoidance affines by the fact of his marrying their daughter.",joking kin,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:25:29.476994+00:00
1349,/san_silberbauer_151_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,a boy,kin_role,"ma:sa (fz, mbw)",kin_role,kinship,Text explicitly identifies boy and ma:sa as joking kin before conversion to avoidance affines.,"According to my informants, a boy would treat his babama (MB, FZH) and his ma:sa (fz, mbw) as avoidance kin as soon as he began to court their daughter, anticipating their conversion from joking kin to avoidance affines by the fact of his marrying their daughter.",joking kin,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:25:29.476994+00:00
1350,/san_silberbauer_156_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,the offending husband or wife,person,his or her joking partners,group,within_group,Text reports culturally recognized public teasing by 'joking partners' of an adulterous spouse within the band.,"An adulterous spouse is quietly told by friends to mend his or her ways, or if it can be done without precipitating marital disaster, the offending husband or wife is publicly teased by his or her joking partners.",joking partners,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.8,Document names 'joking partners' but does not specify kin roles or named corporate units; coded as within_group patterned teasing.,2026-07-06T10:25:36.175347+00:00
1351,/san_silberbauer_161_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,husband,kin_role,his wife's kin group,kin_role,kinship,"Text states a culturally recognized joking/respect status of husband within wife's kin, a recurring kinship-patterned relation.","The husband comes under the tutelage of his wife's father in a dependent role, which approximates that of a child in the family. The joking/respect status of the husband within his wife's kin group is the same as hers and vice versa.",joking/respect status,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:25:43.693438+00:00
1352,/san_silberbauer_165_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,elder brother,kin_role,younger brother,kin_role,kinship,Text states same-sex siblings' relationship includes recurrent joking and respect.,"Consistent with this vicarious authority, the relationship between same-sex siblings before the younger attains independent status is a mixture of joking and respect.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:25:55.671286+00:00
1353,/san_silberbauer_165_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,elder sister,kin_role,younger sister,kin_role,kinship,Same-sex sister pairs are described as having joking alongside respect and close bonds.,"Consistent with this vicarious authority, the relationship between same-sex siblings before the younger attains independent status is a mixture of joking and respect.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:25:55.671286+00:00
1354,/san_silberbauer_165_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,junior sister,kin_role,young spouses,group,kinship,"Text explicitly calls the junior sister a 'joking partner' of the young spouses, a recurring kinship role.","A junior sister, by contrast, is a joking partner of both the young spouses and spends a good deal of time with them, reinforcing the bond of same-sex siblinghood.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.95,,2026-07-06T10:25:55.671286+00:00
1355,/san_silberbauer_172_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,≠ xwa:,person,N/udukhwe,person,kinship,Text describes recurrent licensed criticism between classificatory brothers; joking relationship anchored in kin role.,“There are men so mean as to deny meat to a gjiba:xuma [younger brother] who has helped all day with work.” ... (≠ xwa: and N/udukhwe were classificatory brothers).,joking relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:26:03.918111+00:00
1356,/san_silberbauer_173_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,joking partners,group,migrants,group,within_group,Text shows culturally patterned teasing by 'joking partners' used to publically pressure migrants within the band.,"His joking partners sniped away at him without result, but matters came to a head over some arrows he had borrowed without returning and his refusal to make any gifts of meat to the owner, contrary to custom.",joking partners,,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,Patterned teasing used instrumentally to 'ease out' offenders; migrants were the recurring targets in this example.,2026-07-06T10:26:17.414300+00:00
1357,/san_silberbauer_173_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,N/udukhwe,person,classificatory elder brother,kin_role,kinship,"Verbal duel context describes interaction with a classificatory elder brother, indicating a patterned kin-role verbal relationship.",N/udukhwe had shown restraint toward his classificatory elder brother by addressing his complaint to a third party and avoiding direct confrontation.,,,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.6,"Passage implies recurrent, role-based verbal duel behavior between classificatory siblings; example involves a named person.",2026-07-06T10:26:17.414300+00:00
1358,/san_silberbauer_180_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,visiting band,group,home band,group,within_group,Text reports recurrent joking partners across band boundaries within band alliances.,"Having numerical superiority and also a generally “pushing” manner, they dominated the home band after a few weeks. The remarks of joking partners across band boundaries became more and more pointed, cooperative ventures virtually ceased, and games, dances, and discussion increasingly became one-band occasions.",,,mixed,joking_relationship,0.9,Extracted as band-level joking partnership within the same society's inter-band alliances; visitors vs. home band roles implied.,2026-07-06T10:26:25.810918+00:00
1359,/san_silberbauer_236_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,joking relative,kin_role,avoidance relatives,kin_role,kinship,Text contrasts culturally recognized 'joking' vs 'avoidance' kin with different borrowing liberties.,"Avoidance relatives may borrow “general use” artifacts after asking permission, but a joking relative may borrow without the formality of a request.",licensed liberties / borrowing without formality,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.9,The passage frames 'joking relative' as an institutionalized kin role contrasted with 'avoidance relatives' regarding permitted familiar behavior.,2026-07-06T10:26:33.327333+00:00
1360,/san_silberbauer_238_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,joking relatives,kin_role,joking relatives,kin_role,kinship,"Text describes recurring, obligated teasing/gifting between 'joking relatives' as a cultural institution tied to kin roles.","Joking relatives are obliged to grant each others' requests for goods and services and to give these priority over normal (i.e., other) exchange obligations.",joking relatives,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:26:42.119310+00:00
1361,/san_silberbauer_254_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,initiation mates,age_set,joking partners,group,within_group,"Text explicitly links initiation mates with a recurrent circle of joking partners, a culturally patterned exchange network.","This, then, is comparable with the generalized-balanced reciprocity that occurs in the circle of initiation mates, joking partners, and others.","circle of initiation mates, joking partners",,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.8,,2026-07-06T10:26:54.008935+00:00
1362,/san_silberbauer_296_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,joking relatives,kin_role,joking partners,kin_role,kinship,"Text describes culturally patterned, recurrent teasing between kin-role 'joking relatives' as 'joking partners'.","In this context joking relatives function as feedback loops that provide an individual with information about others' reactions to his behavior, reducing randomness both in his behavior and his anticipation of its social consequences. The exchanges of joking partners include opportunity for making amends and for extending forgiveness, which, because it is a public performance, gives emotional comfort not only to the partners but to the whole band as well.",joking partners / joking relatives,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.6,Document uses general kin-role categories rather than naming specific lineages or villages; coded as kinship-level institutionalized joking.,2026-07-06T10:27:03.131510+00:00
1363,/san_silberbauer_302_1981_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,one woman,kin_role,the husband of another,kin_role,kinship,"Text contrasts restricted speech toward another man's wife with greater freedom toward her husband, indicating institutionalized liberties.","Although I must be circumspect in my communicative behavior toward another man's wife, I am allowed considerable freedom when talking to her husband.",,,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.6,Document frames differential licensed liberties tied to kinship roles (restrained toward another's wife; freer with her husband).,2026-07-06T10:27:12.260191+00:00
1364,/san_silberbauer_310_1972_sv,SouthernAfrica,san,kin,kin_role,kin (permitted playmates),kin_role,kinship,Text states kin relationships are categorized into joking (ho:khwudi) allowing 'play' between kin.,"Relationships between kin are categorized as either joking (ho:khwudi) or avoidance (gjiukxekxu), and an individual distinguishes between those of his kin whom he should !ao (fear, respect) and those with whom he may “play.”",joking (ho:khwudi),ho:khwudi,unclear,joking_relationship,0.8,"Document gives a categorical institutionalized joking relationship among kin but does not specify particular kin roles (e.g., mother's brother, cross-cousin).",2026-07-06T10:27:19.336321+00:00
