598,/Hausa_Baba_138_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,husband,person,his joking relations,group,within_group,"Text names recurrent 'joking relations' who assist husband in ritual work, indicating an institutionalized joking tie within the society.","Then at the seventh month, or earlier, the husband begins to cut down wood in the bush and collect it, he and his younger brother and his joking relations.",,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.6,Document uses the phrase 'his joking relations' as a recognized social category allied with husband; parties not further named.,2026-07-06T09:18:03.827094+00:00
599,/Hausa_Baba_145_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,wife,kin_role,husband's younger brother,kin_role,kinship,Text states wives joking with husband's younger brother as a culturally patterned relation.,"You joke with his younger brother, and you joke with all your husband's joking relations—his grandparents and cross-cousins.",joke with,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:18:12.585478+00:00
600,/Hausa_Baba_145_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,wife,kin_role,husband's grandparents,kin_role,kinship,Grandparents are listed among the husband's 'joking relations' with whom the wife jokes recurrently.,"You joke with his younger brother, and you joke with all your husband's joking relations—his grandparents and cross-cousins.",joking relations,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:18:12.585478+00:00
601,/Hausa_Baba_145_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,wife,kin_role,husband's cross-cousins,kin_role,kinship,Cross-cousins are explicitly named as part of the husband's joking relations with the wife.,"You joke with his younger brother, and you joke with all your husband's joking relations—his grandparents and cross-cousins.",joking relations,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:18:12.585478+00:00
602,/Hausa_Baba_151_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,Uwa,person,Baba,person,kinship,"Text explicitly calls Uwa 'my kawa' — kawa is a named joking partnership, a recurrent kin-based tie.",Uwa was my kawa .,kawa,kawa,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.8,,2026-07-06T09:18:24.615510+00:00
603,/Hausa_Baba_151_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,Giwa,person,Audu,person,kinship,Giwa 'persuaded her joking relation' Audu — explicitly described as a culturally recognized joking relation between named kin.,"Very well, Giwa consulted with her husband's younger brother Audu, she coaxed him, she persuaded her joking relation, they talked the matter over until he agreed.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.7,Audu is identified as the husband's younger brother; the joking tie is described between Giwa and Audu.,2026-07-06T09:18:24.615510+00:00
