608,/Hausa_Baba_243_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,grandparents,kin_role,grandchildren,kin_role,kinship,Text states grandparents act as joking relations with grandchildren; clearly a kinship-based licensed teasing role.,"Talle is chosen to act as ‘grandmother’ as she is a joking relation of ‘Yardada’s, as also are grandparents. This joking relationship is of the kind between ethnic and occupational groups, not between real kinsfolk.",joking relation (grandmother–grandchild role),,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:18:59.996879+00:00
609,/Hausa_Baba_243_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,"Buzaye, the Sokoto people",ethnic group,blacksmiths,caste,within_group,Author explicitly describes joking as between ethnic (Buzaye/Sokoto) and occupational (blacksmith) groups; patterned cross-unit teasing.,"'Yardada a daughter of the Buzaye, the Sokoto people, so won’t she joke with a blacksmith’s daughter? ... Talle is chosen to act as ‘grandmother’ as she is a joking relation of ‘Yardada’s, as also are grandparents. This joking relationship is of the kind between ethnic and occupational groups, not between real kinsfolk.",joking relation (ethnic–occupational),,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:18:59.996879+00:00
610,/Hausa_Baba_24_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,Fulani,ethnic group,Kanuri (Barebare),ethnic group,cross_group,Text explicitly calls Fulani–Kanuri a culturally defined 'joking relation' between ethnic groups.,"The second classification of Hausa marriages distinguishes primarily
between marriages of kinship or quasi-kinship and marriages between

unrelated persons. The former type ( auren zumunci, auren dangintaka )
includes all forms of cousin-marriage, and holds between members of
different occupational or even ethnic groups which are defined as joking
relations, such as the Fulani and the Kanuri (Barebare).",joking relations,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:19:06.456188+00:00
