634,/Hausa_Greenberg_203_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,cross-cousins,kin_role,each other,kin_role,kinship,Text states cross-cousins are culturally designated 'playmates' with licensed liberties.,"Although the kinship terminology, which is in general of the merging type, gives no special recognition to cross- cousins as opposed to parallel cousins, cross cousins, whether of the same or opposite sex, are said to be ’abó[unknown]kán wa[unknown]sá[unknown], “playmates.”",’abó[unknown]kán wa[unknown]sá[unknown] (playmates),’abó[unknown]kán wa[unknown]sá[unknown],non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,"Text describes superior/inferior privileges (taking property), making relation asymmetrical in practice.",2026-07-06T09:21:26.607951+00:00
