674,/Hausa_Smith_44_NK,WesternAfrica,Hausa,spouses of Ego’s elder siblings of different sex,kin_role,Ego,person,kinship,"Text notes joking ties between Ego and spouses of elder siblings as tension-relieving, recurrent.","Joking relationships between the spouses of Ego’s elder siblings of different sex and Ego, and also between the abokan wasa (cross-cousins and grandparents, particularly the former) of a spouse and his partner by marriage, tend to relieve the tensions inherent in affinal relationships and the conditions of Hausa marriage.",,abokan wasa,mixed,joking_relationship,0.85,Entity labels follow phrasing in text; relation framed as recurring in marriage context.,2026-07-06T09:24:22.960903+00:00
