735,/Kanuri_Cohen_74_NK,WesternAfrica,Kanuri,Grandparents,kin_role,Grandchildren,kin_role,kinship,Text describes recurrent joking (suli) between grandparents and grandchildren as a patterned kinship relation.,"There is a high degree of expressive and affective fondness found in the joking relationships between grandparents and grandchildren which centers, as we have seen, most intensively around the namesake attribute of the same relationship. ... It does not show up in the questionnaire data summarized in Table I, because the joking relations ( suli ) with grandparents already includes friendship behaviour within its meaning content for this particular category of relative.",joking relations,suli,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:29:05.761085+00:00
736,/Kanuri_Rosman_194_NK,WesternAfrica,Kanuri,jili,clan,linked jili,clan,within_group,Text describes recurrent joking/gift exchanges between linked jili (clan group) during festival.,This is also the time when members of the various jili give small gifts to members of linked jili with whom they have joking Age Stratification relationships ( n[unknown]ngima ).,joking Age Stratification relationships,n[unknown]ngima,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.6,Document gives no specific clan names; extracted generic paired unit as 'jili' linked to 'linked jili'.,2026-07-06T09:29:12.520850+00:00
737,/Katab_Meek_32_NK,WesternAfrica,Katab,A Katab,ethnic group,his cousins,kin_role,kinship,Text states Katab are on playmate terms with all his cousins; kinship-based joking institution.,"A Katab appears to be, to some extent, on playmate terms with all his cousins, but he will never play with a female cousin whose potential guardian he is, that is to say, whom he will one day give in marriage.",playmate relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.95,,2026-07-06T09:29:25.542040+00:00
738,/Katab_Meek_32_NK,WesternAfrica,Katab,A Katab,ethnic group,ortho-cousins,kin_role,kinship,"Text explicitly identifies ortho-cousins as playmates (albeit 'modified'), indicating an institutionalized joking tie.",But ortho-cousins are only playmates in a modified sense.,playmate relationship (modified),,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,Described as a modified form of the general cousin playmate relationship.,2026-07-06T09:29:25.542040+00:00
739,/Katab_Meek_32_NK,WesternAfrica,Katab,a man,person,his wife's brother's wife,kin_role,kinship,"Text states a man may be playmates with his wife's brother's wife when she belongs to a different clan, a patterned affinal joking tie.","The playmate relationship may exist between a man and his wife's brother's wife, but only if she belongs to some clan other than his own; for a woman of the same clan is a sister, and the joking relationship with a sister is not permissible.",playmate relationship (affinal),,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,Condition: only when the affinal woman belongs to a different clan; same-clan affinal treated as sister (no joking).,2026-07-06T09:29:25.542040+00:00
740,/Kpelle_Bellman_187_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,ngala,kin_role,maling,kin_role,kinship,Text explicitly describes ngala–maling as daily joking 'play husband and wife' relationship tied to kin roles.,"In the first generation the ngala and maling treat each other as ‘play husband and wife’ in a daily joking relationship whereby sexual play with each other is permitted, but they are prohibited from having sexual intercourse.",play husband and wife; daily joking relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.95,,2026-07-06T09:29:36.054916+00:00
741,/Kpelle_Bellman_22_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,ngala,kin_role,maling,kin_role,kinship,"Text describes recurring, culturally sanctioned joking rights between ngala and maling kin roles.","Besides the serious or formal rights and obligations between ngala and maling, other aspects of the relationship are expressed as joking behavior between kinsmen. When drinking palm wine, the maling is “to take off the dirt” by taking the first drink, whereas the ngala gets the last dregs from the bottom of the gourd; the maling is permitted to take any of the ngala's clothes without asking, while the ngala can take the maling's hat; and where there are not enough seats available, the maling will stand and offer the chair to his ngala.",ngala-maling relationship,ngala-maling,mixed,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:29:42.831600+00:00
742,/Kpelle_Bellman_24_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,Folpahzoi,person,Walawulu,person,within_group,"Repeated, culturally recognized ngala-maling joking tie between these two Poro initiates.","Folpahzoi and Walawulu had joined the Poro together about thirty-five years before and since that time been close friends, a bond expressed through the ngala-maling joking relationship. When Folpahzoi and Walawulu interact, they use the relationship to locate their informal rights within the setting.",ngala-maling joking relationship,ngala-maling,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.95,Example pair illustrating the institutionalized joking tie between members who were co-initiates in Poro.,2026-07-06T09:29:52.177771+00:00
743,/Kpelle_Bellman_24_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,ngala,kin_role,maling,kin_role,within_group,Text describes culturally patterned rights and licensed teasing tied to ngala/maling relational statuses.,"Although each can be ngala or maling depending on the technique of reckoning, each argues that he is the maling to the other. By making the other ngala, the speaker is entitled to take the first drink of palm wine or cane juice (raw rum) and can even take wine from the other's palm tree without permission.",ngala-maling,ngala; maling,mixed,joking_relationship,0.9,"Roles provide licensed liberties (first drink, taking wine, joking abuse); symmetry coded mixed because each may claim maling but rights are role-based.",2026-07-06T09:29:52.177771+00:00
744,/Kpelle_Bellman_87_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,initiates,age_set,men,group,within_group,Recurring teasing of boys by adult men during initiation rituals — institutionalized ritual joking.,"Before the initiations, there is a great deal of joking and teasing of the initiates about their having to do battle with the devil (an example is presented in the next chapter).",teasing during initiation,,non_symmetric,teasing,0.9,Initiates treated as an age-set/categorical social unit; men are adult ritual performers exercising licensed teasing.,2026-07-06T09:29:58.263178+00:00
745,/Kpelle_Erchak_42_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,Ego,kin_role,ngkela (mother's brother),kin_role,kinship,"Text explicitly calls ego–mother's brother a classic joking relationship (licensed teasing, favors).","Ego's relationship with any one of these, Avuncular And but especially with his ngkela (mother's brother) or maleng (cross-cousin) is a classic jokingrelationship: one can ask the other for favors and material things, make sexual and other jokes, and so forth.",classic jokingrelationship,ngkela,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:30:15.318542+00:00
746,/Kpelle_Erchak_42_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,Ego,kin_role,father's sister,kin_role,kinship,Father's sister is listed with mother's brother and cross-cousins as 'play wives/play husbands' and part of joking ties with ego.,"Ego's mother's brother, father's sister, and cross- Kinship Terminology cousins, and a bifurcate merging avuncular terminology. A listing of some kin-terms and their denotata can be found in Bellman (1975: – ). Certain rules of behavior are associated with this terminology. Ego's mother's brother, father's sister, and cross-cousins, are referred to as “play wives” or “play husbands” depending on ego's sex.",play wife/play husband,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.85,,2026-07-06T09:30:15.318542+00:00
747,/Kpelle_Erchak_42_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,Ego,kin_role,maleng (cross-cousin),kin_role,kinship,Cross-cousins (maleng) are named as 'play spouses' and part of the classic joking relationship with ego.,"Ego's relationship with any one of these, Avuncular And but especially with his ngkela (mother's brother) or maleng (cross-cousin) is a classic jokingrelationship: one can ask the other for favors and material things, make sexual and other jokes, and so forth.",play wife/play husband,maleng,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:30:15.318542+00:00
748,/Kpelle_Erchak_42_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,mother's brother,kin_role,sister's son,kin_role,kinship,The mother's brother–sister's son tie is described as the much-studied patrilineal relationship and enjoyed by both parties.,"A man and his sister's son enjoy the much-studied patrilineal43 African mother's brother-sister's son Cousins relationship, and a man must give his approval of and be one of the overseers of, the marriage of his sister's daughter, at least in Nyafokwele chiefdom.",mother's brother–sister's son relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.8,,2026-07-06T09:30:15.318542+00:00
749,/Kpelle_Lancy_143_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,the “elders”,group,the Humor speaker,person,within_group,Elders repeatedly use jokes/proverbs in disputes to wound a named disputant (institutionalized role-based teasing).,"The “elders” in a dispute add two substantial speech elements to the contest, jokes and proverbs. These jokes and proverbs are designed to wound the Humor speaker, to lower his or her esteem in the eyes of the audience.",elders' joking in disputes,,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:30:24.124867+00:00
750,/Kpelle_Lancy_143_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,young boys,age_set,another boy,person,within_group,Play among boys features recurring joking practices where boys target other boys (patterned age-based teasing).,"The use of joking is begun early by young boys, and at times it is difficult to distinguish between joking and abusing, A boy may make a joke about another boy, “He walks like a goat,” which evokes laughter from other boys in the group.",boys' teasing in play,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.85,,2026-07-06T09:30:24.124867+00:00
751,/Kpelle_Lancy_82_NK,WesternAfrica,Kpelle,second older,kin_role,unconvinced party (holdout),group,within_group,"Recurring, culturally patterned teasing by elders in trials directed at holdouts; institutionalized courtroom joking.","Joking is another type of speech event, and the purpose is to make the position of the “unconvinced party” or “holdout” look ridiculous. Several Humor examples occur in this trial. When the second older calls for drinks he is signaling that Gbokpele is wasting their time and that, by his obstinance, he has turned a serious trial into a farce.",joking in trials,,non_symmetric,teasing,0.8,"Text treats joking as a recurrent, sanctioned speech event in trials; elder role (second older) teases holdout.",2026-07-06T09:30:33.358953+00:00
818,/MOssi_195_NK,WesternAfrica,MOssi,Mossi,ethnic group,Gourounsi,ethnic group,cross_group,Text describes recurrent joking label applied by Mossi to Gourounsi; cross-ethnic institutionalized teasing.,"Mossi often jokingly refer to the Gourounsi as their ligidi (meaning money), implying their status as individuals to be sold as slaves.",,ligidi,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:38:28.405496+00:00
819,/MOssi_195_NK,WesternAfrica,MOssi,Mogho,ethnic group,Samogho,ethnic group,within_group,Author explicitly calls a joking relationship between Mogho and Samogho; presented as a recurrent cultural tie.,"The joking relationship between Mogho and Samogho is more nearly symmetrical. Both groups declare that their two ancestors quarreled over the bones of a dog, and this quarrel still continues.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:38:28.405496+00:00
854,/Mende_Little_130_NK,WesternAfrica,Mende,brother,kin_role,sister,kin_role,kinship,Text explicitly states a culturally recognized joking relationship between brother and sister; clearly kinship-based.,"There is a strong joking relationship between brother and sister, but a brother who sits on his sister's bed may be held guilty of simongama (i.e. incest, see Chapter VII).",strong joking relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.95,,2026-07-06T09:43:04.354840+00:00
855,/Mossi_262_NK,WesternAfrica,Mossi,mother's brother's wife,kin_role,Ego,kin_role,kinship,"Text describes a recurrent, asymmetrical joking tie between mother's brother's wife and Ego.","However, joking in this relationship is asymmetrical. The mother's brother's wife takes the more aggressive role, and from the vehemence of her joking, and the structural nature of the relationship, it appears likely that amity lies less heavily in the balance than hostility.",Avuncular,,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:43:23.922231+00:00
856,/Mossi_262_NK,WesternAfrica,Mossi,Siblings-in-law,kin_role,Siblings-in-law,kin_role,kinship,"Author treats joking between siblings-in-law as a culturally patterned, reciprocal institution linking kin groups.","Joking between siblings-in-law who are potential spouses, yet are presently constrained by a prohibition against adultery, has frequently been ascribed the function of reducing tension in a situation of conflict. The kin groups of siblings-in-law are always structurally equivalent because groups occupying significantly different strata in Mossi society do not intermarry.",Siblings-In-Law,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:43:23.922231+00:00
857,/Mossi_262_NK,WesternAfrica,Mossi,Sibs (or lineages),lineage,other Sibs (or lineages),lineage,within_group,"Descent groups (sibs/lineages) are described as having established, reciprocal joking alliances between them.","Sibs (or lineages) whose members joke with one another are, of course, also separate groups. They are always united by a strong tradition of reciprocal social and economic aid. The origin of joking relationships between two descent groups is often ascribed to the alleged fact that, when they first arrived in the village, leaders of both falsely claimed to the chief that he and his kinsmen had arrived first...",joking alliance,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,Text frames these as between distinct descent groups (lineages/sibs) within the same society.,2026-07-06T09:43:23.922231+00:00
858,/Mossi_262_NK,WesternAfrica,Mossi,age-sets,age_set,other age-sets within an age-grade,age_set,within_group,"Joking between age-sets is presented as a recurring, role-based feature of age-grade life-cycle and activities.",Joking between age-sets within an age-grade varies with the generational position of the set in Mossi society. In the years immediately following initiation the members are much involved in group activities... and during this period joking is important.,,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.85,Symmetry varies by generational position; text does not specify uniform symmetry.,2026-07-06T09:43:23.922231+00:00
859,/Mossi_Hammon_261_KS,WesternAfrica,Mossi,mother's brother,kin_role,Ego,kin_role,kinship,Text describes a culturally patterned avuncular joking tie; asymmetrical teasing permitted between maternal uncle and nephew.,"The ambivalence in the relationship is manifested not
only by joking, which is asymmetrical—with Ego being the more aggressive—
but by theft as well. Perhaps as partial compensation for his inability to inherit
matrilaterally, Ego is permitted to steal his mother's brother's property during
his lifetime and can also make off with the beer and some of the animals
collected for his funeral.",Joking with the Mother's Brother,,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:43:31.752271+00:00
860,/Mossi_Hammon_261_KS,WesternAfrica,Mossi,mother's brother's wife,kin_role,Ego,kin_role,kinship,"Author treats joking with maternal uncle's wife as a separate, recurring permissive relationship tied to kinship roles.","Joking between Ego and his mother's brother's wife is to be regarded as a
separate relationship because of her nonmembership in the mother's brother's
descent group, but certain of the structural circumstances are similar.",Joking with the Mother's Brother's Wife,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.9,Symmetry not specified; treated as distinct institutionalized joking tie.,2026-07-06T09:43:31.752271+00:00
