868,/Mossi_Hammond_260_NK,WesternAfrica,Mossi,Ego,kin_role,his mother's agnatic kin,kin_role,kinship,Explicitly listed institutionalized joking tie between Ego and mother's agnatic kin; clearly kinship-based.,"Among the Mossi, joking is institutionalized as an adjustive mechanism in the following relationships: (1) between Ego and his mother's agnatic kin, particularly his mother's elder brother; (2) between Ego and his mother's brother's wife; (3) between siblings-in-law; (4) between sibs; (5) between age-sets in the same age-grade; (6) between certain villages; and (7) between the Mossi and several other ethnic groups.",,,unclear,joking_relationship,0.85,,2026-07-06T09:44:25.648565+00:00
869,/Mossi_Hammond_260_NK,WesternAfrica,Mossi,Ego,kin_role,his mother's elder brother,kin_role,kinship,Text highlights mother's elder brother as a particular recurring joking partner of Ego; kin-role relationship.,"Among the Mossi, joking is institutionalized as an adjustive mechanism in the following relationships: (1) between Ego and his mother's agnatic kin, particularly his mother's elder brother; (2) between Ego and his mother's brother's wife; (3) between siblings-in-law; (4) between sibs; (5) between age-sets in the same age-grade; (6) between certain villages; and (7) between the Mossi and several other ethnic groups.",,,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.8,Mother's elder brother likely higher-status; asymmetry inferred from general discussion.,2026-07-06T09:44:25.648565+00:00
