876,/Mossi_Hammond_262_KS,WesternAfrica,Mossi,mother's brother's wife,kin_role,Ego (nephew),kin_role,kinship,Text describes recurrent asymmetric joking between a mother's brother's wife and her nephew; clearly kinship-based.,"However, joking in this relationship is asymmetrical. The mother's brother's wife takes the more aggressive role, and from the vehemence of her joking, and the structural nature of the relationship, it appears likely that amity lies less heavily in the balance than hostility.",Avuncular And Nepotic,,non_symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:44:41.844958+00:00
877,/Mossi_Hammond_262_KS,WesternAfrica,Mossi,Siblings-in-law,kin_role,Siblings-in-law,kin_role,kinship,"Text treats joking between siblings-in-law as a recurring, reciprocal, socially recognized relationship tied to marriage rules.",Siblings-in-law who joke are separated by the rule of sib exogamy observed among the Mossi. Reciprocity is basic to the marriage contract that unites their respective king groups.,Siblings-In-Law,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:44:41.844958+00:00
