984,/Tallensi_17_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,grandparent,kin_role,grandchild,kin_role,kinship,"Text describes a recurrent, permitted joking (mutual ragging) specifically between grandparents and grandchildren.","In this case equality, comatibility and partisanship, as if in league against the generation between them, are emphasized, more particularly by the joking relationship—mutual ragging among the Tallensi—permitted between grandparent and grandchild.",mutual ragging / joking relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:57:29.026139+00:00
985,/Tallensi_Forte_236_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,paternal grandparents,kin_role,grandchild,kin_role,kinship,Text states paternal grandparents and grandchildren reciprocally tease as an institutionalized relation.,"This joking relationship holds for both sets of grandparents, and serves the purpose of reconciling the potentially conflicting elements in their relationships.",joking relationship,ba-kpeem / ma-kpeem / yaab / yaab-p(ɔ)k,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:57:53.181666+00:00
986,/Tallensi_Forte_236_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,maternal grandparents,kin_role,grandchild,kin_role,kinship,"Author explicitly states that the joking relationship holds with both sets of grandparents, including maternal.","This joking relationship holds for both sets of grandparents, and serves the purpose of reconciling the potentially conflicting elements in their relationships.",joking relationship,ba-kpeem / ma-kpeem / yaab / yaab-p(ɔ)k,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:57:53.181666+00:00
987,/Tallensi_Forte_236_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,patrilineal grandparent,kin_role,grandchild of the same sex,kin_role,kinship,Text notes greater intimacy and patterned joking particularly between patrilineal grandparent and same-sex grandchild.,"With it goes an intimacy and mutual trust, more particularly between patrilineal grandparent and grandchild of the same sex, such as is not found between any other kinsfolk, close or distant.",privileged familiarity / joking,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.85,,2026-07-06T09:57:53.181666+00:00
988,/Tallensi_Forte_236_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,siblings-in-law,kin_role,each other,kin_role,kinship,Author cites similar usage of joking between siblings-in-law as an institutional pattern.,"Cf. the similar usage between siblings-in-law, p. . Joking in the present case reconciles the familiarity permissible on the grounds of personal interest and the social equivalence of alternate generations, with the respect due to grandparents because of their age and their lineage status.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.6,Cf. indicates similar institutionalized joking; source reference incomplete in text.,2026-07-06T09:57:53.181666+00:00
