992,/Tallensi_Fortes_197_nk,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,grandparent,kin_role,grandchild,kin_role,kinship,Text states teasing occurs between grandparent and grandchild; kinship-based recurring licence.,"You cannot tease or joke with your parent or your child, the Tallensi say, because you do so with your grandparent or grandchild.",,kooh,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:58:17.570658+00:00
993,/Tallensi_Fortes_197_nk,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,parent,kin_role,child,kin_role,kinship,Text explicitly prohibits teasing between parent and child as a cultural rule (institutionalized avoidance).,"In particular, the familiarity between parents and children never goes so far as mutual teasing, as in a joking relationship. If a native is asked about this he frowns and says that it would be most offensive for a son or daughter to tease or joke with (kooh) a parent or vice versa.",,kooh,symmetric,avoidance,0.95,Prohibition described as normative cultural rule rather than casual; included as institutionalized avoidance.,2026-07-06T09:58:17.570658+00:00
994,/Tallensi_Fortes_207_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,parents' parents,kin_role,Grandchildren,kin_role,kinship,Text explicitly states grandchildren have a joking relationship with their grandparents.,"Deference and respect for their conjugal privacy, amounting to a mild avoidance associated with the incest taboo is proper in relation to parents. But with parents' parents one has a joking relationship, which reconciles respect for the paternal grandfather's authority with the affectionate trust in the relationship of alternate generations...",joking relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.95,,2026-07-06T09:58:31.831692+00:00
