996,/Tallensi_Fortes_207_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,Father's mother,kin_role,child,kin_role,kinship,"Text describes father's mother as indulgent and part of the affectionate, joking relations with younger generation.","Father's mother is the acme of indulgence, for unlike mother she never has to forbid or scold and feels no Techniques Of responsibility for a child's conduct.",,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.85,Implied joking/affectional liberties between father's mother and grandchildren/children.,2026-07-06T09:58:31.831692+00:00
997,/Tallensi_Fortes_222_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,grandparents,kin_role,grandchildren,kin_role,kinship,"Text explicitly states a classical, culturally recognized joking relationship between these kin roles.","As in many tribal societies, and consistently with this point of view, the restraint that is customary between parents and children is counterbalanced by a classical joking relationship between grandparents and grandchildren.",classical joking relationship,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:58:36.911875+00:00
998,/Tallensi_Fortes_273_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,a man,kin_role,his wife's siblings (in the widest classificatory sense of all her clan-siblings),kin_role,kinship,Text describes a conventionalized joking relationship between a man and his wife's (classificatory) siblings.,"Conventionalized joking between a man and his wife's siblings (in the widest classificatory sense of all her clan-siblings), and of a woman with her husband's sisters and his more distant clansmen, is another indication of the social equivalence of siblings.",Conventionalized joking,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T09:58:56.851641+00:00
999,/Tallensi_Fortes_273_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,a woman,kin_role,her husband's sisters,kin_role,kinship,Author explicitly notes patterned joking of a woman with her husband's sisters (sister-in-law relations).,"Conventionalized joking between a man and his wife's siblings (in the widest classificatory sense of all her clan-siblings), and of a woman with her husband's sisters and his more distant clansmen, is another indication of the social equivalence of siblings.",Conventionalized joking,,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,Also evidenced by reciprocal address terms 'our wife' and 'husband' between wife's and husband's kin.,2026-07-06T09:58:56.851641+00:00
