1011,/Tallensi_Fortes_91_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,man,kin_role,wife's brother (dakii),kin_role,kinship,Text compares clan joking with affinal teasing; gives man teasing his wife's brother (dakii) as routine.,"As we have noted, the natives compare them with the joking relationship of affines of the same generation. A man will tease his wife's brother (dakii) or sister (dakii-p(ɔ)k) or his sister's husband (dakii) or a clansman's wife in this way, and a woman her brother's wife (p(ɔ)□akii) or her husband's sister (p(ɔ)□akii), to the amusement of both.",affinal teasing,dakii,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:00:16.870891+00:00
1012,/Tallensi_Fortes_91_NK,WesternAfrica,Tallensi,man,kin_role,sister's husband (dakii),kin_role,kinship,Author states men routinely tease their sister's husband (dakii) as part of affinal joking.,"A man will tease his wife's brother (dakii) or sister (dakii-p(ɔ)k) or his sister's husband (dakii) or a clansman's wife in this way, and a woman her brother's wife (p(ɔ)□akii) or her husband's sister (p(ɔ)□akii), to the amusement of both.",affinal teasing,dakii,symmetric,joking_relationship,0.9,,2026-07-06T10:00:16.870891+00:00
